  "findings": [
    {
      "evidence": "design.md says the launcher uses `npx --yes ...@<pinned>` \"or a resolvable `srt` binary whose `--version` matches; a mismatch is an explicit refusal\". The spec says the launch is refused \"when the pinned sandbox runtime ... is unavailable\". `template/scripts/sandboxed_writer.py` `srt_launcher()` (diff lines 319-322) checks only `shutil.which(\"npx\")` and returns the npx command. It never resolves an `srt` binary or checks its version. A failure to fetch or run the runtime would surface only as a non-zero exit from the launched process, not as a pre-launch refusal. The pinned-version string is covered by `test_launcher_pinned_and_requires_npx`, but the runtime-unavailable and version-mismatch refusals are not.",
      "id": "pinned-runtime-availability-not-checked",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The design and spec require an explicit refusal when the pinned sandbox runtime is unavailable or mismatched. The launcher only checks that `npx` is on PATH and does not verify the runtime itself."
    }
  ],
